.TH UNHEADED\-CLI 1 "2026-10-29" "unheaded 84b3253f" "Unheaded Kingdom"
.SH NAME
unheaded\-cli \- THE GAUNTLETS \- Command\-line interface for the Unheaded Kingdom
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unheaded\-cli
[\fIOPTION\fR]...
COMMAND [ARG]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
THE GAUNTLETS \- Command\-line interface for the Unheaded Kingdom

  \- Containers: desired state through Cuirass (list, create, delete, inspect)
  \- Services: health from Akira's consensus, logs from the dashboard
  \- Status: both of the above in one overview
  \- Configuration: get, set, validate CLI settings and contexts
  \- Generate: IaC artifact generation (Ansible, Terraform, K8s, etc.)
  \- Observe: observability backend configuration
  \- API keys: create, list, revoke uhk_ keys for automation (ADR\-103)

Secrets and network commands, and container start/stop/exec and service
deploy/restart/scale, fail: no Unheaded service provides them yet.

Use "unheaded <command> \-\-help" for more information about a command.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B apikey
Create, list and revoke API keys (uhk_) for automation
.TP
.B completion
Generate shell completion scripts
.TP
.B config
Manage CLI configuration
.TP
.B container
Manage containers
.TP
.B generate
Generate IaC artifacts
.TP
.B network
Network policies and routes (not available)
.TP
.B observe
Manage observability backends
.TP
.B secret
Manage secrets
.TP
.B service
Service health and logs
.TP
.B status
Show system status overview
.TP
.B token
Print a 5\-minute service token for one service (for curl)
.TP
.B version
Show version information
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-context \fISTRING\fR
Context to use (default local)
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable color output
.TP
.B \-o \fISTRING\fR
Output format (short) (default table)
.TP
.B \-\-output \fISTRING\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml, wide (default table)
.TP
.B \-q
Suppress non\-essential output (short)
.TP
.B \-\-quiet
Suppress non\-essential output
.TP
.B \-v
Enable verbose output (short)
.TP
.B \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
display this help and exit
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
output version information and exit
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unheaded (1)
